    "n-h02": {"x": 492, "y": 2355, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "app", "text": "H-02 · Tap a card opens the editor. ⋮ opens H-03. Long-press a card = same menu (accessibility shortcut). Grid keeps 2 columns at 360 dp; covers keep their own 9:16 or 1:1 ratio so columns are masonry-free: card height = cover + 48 dp meta. FAB hides on scroll down, shows on scroll up."},
    "n-e03": {"x": 984, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "editor", "text": "E-03 · Drag anywhere on the timeline = scrub (preview follows, playback pauses). Pinch = zoom (1 s ≈ 32 dp default; max zoom shows single frames on the ruler). Tap a clip/bar selects it; tap empty lane deselects. Bar labels stick to the visible left edge while the bar scrolls off-screen. Mute and + stay pinned; clips slide under a 64 dp Ink0 fade."},
    "n-e04": {"x": 1916, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "editor", "text": "E-04 · Drag a trim handle: the clip resizes live, the badge shows the duration (\"3.2s\"). Edges snap to the playhead, clip edges and beat dots within 8 dp, with one haptic tick per snap. Near the screen edge (48 dp) the timeline auto-scrolls at up to 1 screen/s. Tools act on the selection, or on the clip under the playhead when nothing is selected."},
    "n-panel": {"x": 2408, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "fill": "teal", "page": "editor", "text": "Panel heights · 1-row panels (Volume, Opacity) ~152 dp, 2-row (Filters, Adjust, Speed) ~232–264 dp: the timeline stays. Tall panels (Curves, HSL, Speed curve, Text, Canvas) ~400 dp: the timeline collapses to the main strip only, so the preview keeps ≥ 40% of the height. Sliders apply on release; chips and tiles apply on tap. Done closes; system Back = Done."},
    "n-e05": {"x": 0, "y": 2355, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "editor", "text": "E-05 · Long-press (400 ms) a clip: all clips animate to equal 48 dp squares in a row centred on the finger. The lifted tile scales to 1.1 with an 8 dp shadow and follows the finger; the 3 dp white slot bar shows where it will drop. Each slot change = haptic tick. Release drops and expands back. Drag near edges auto-scrolls."},
    "n-e07": {"x": 984, "y": 2355, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "editor", "text": "E-07 · Select tool enters multi-select: every tap toggles an item (clips, texts, audio). Check badges show membership. Tools in the selection bar apply to all picked items that support them (Speed/Filters skip text). Done or system Back exits; the selection is kept as a single selection of the last item."},
    "n-e08": {"x": 1476, "y": 2355, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "editor", "text": "E-08 · Chip appears only while proxy copies are being made, updates every 1%, and fades out 600 ms after 100%. Editing stays fully usable; preview may stutter until done."},
    "n-t01": {"x": 0, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "clip", "text": "T-01 · Drag either handle on the filmstrip; the preview shows the frame under the handle being dragged. The title updates live (\"Trim · 4.2s\"). Applies on release. Minimum length 0.1 s."},
    "n-t02": {"x": 492, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "clip", "text": "T-02 · Slider is logarithmic: equal distance per doubling (0.1x … 100x). Snaps to preset values within 4 dp with a haptic tick. Value bubble shows while dragging; speed applies on release. Preset chips apply on tap."},
    "n-t03": {"x": 984, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "clip", "text": "T-03 · Drag a beat point vertically to change speed (log scale 0.1x–10x) and horizontally to move it in time. Tap the graph to add a point, long-press a point to remove it. The playhead line on the graph follows the timeline. Editing a preset turns it into Custom."},
    "n-t06": {"x": 2460, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "clip", "text": "T-06 · Tap a tile = apply to the selected clip (or add a 3 s layer at the playhead when nothing is selected). Tap the selected tile again to toggle a before/after peek. Intensity applies on release. Tiles render the current frame through each filter (cached, 60 dp)."},
    "n-t07": {"x": 492, "y": 2355, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "clip", "text": "T-07 · Chip picks which parameter the one slider edits. Changed chips keep their value in the label. Slider is bipolar with a 0 mark and snaps to 0; double-tap the knob resets that parameter. Applies on release. HSL and Curves open their own tall panels (T-08, T-09)."},
    "n-t09": {"x": 1476, "y": 2355, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "clip", "text": "T-09 · Drag a point to move it (x clamped between neighbours). Tap empty area adds a point on the curve; long-press removes (end points can't be removed). Each channel keeps its own curve; edited channels show a dot on their chip."},
    "n-t12": {"x": 0, "y": 3755, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "clip", "text": "T-12 · Crop: drag corners to resize, drag inside to pan the image under the frame. Ratio chips lock the frame. Thirds grid shows while dragging. Mirror and Rotate apply instantly (undoable)."},
    "n-t15": {"x": 1968, "y": 3755, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "clip", "text": "T-15 · One finger drags; two fingers pinch-scale and rotate together. Centre lines snap within 6 dp (mint guide + haptic). Rotation snaps at 0/90/180/270° within 3°. Readout (\"15°\") shows only while rotating."},
    "n-t16": {"x": 2460, "y": 3755, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "clip", "text": "T-16 · Opened by tapping the diamond between two clips (48 dp touch target around a 24 dp glyph). Tiles apply on tap and preview the boundary on loop. Duration capped by the shorter of the two clips. Apply to all sets every boundary."},
    "n-x02": {"x": 492, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "textaudio", "text": "X-02 · Drag the box moves the text; pinch scales; two-finger twist rotates. Corner handles: ✕ delete, ↻ rotate/scale with one finger. Snaps to centre lines (mint). Double-tap the text opens the keyboard in X-01."},
    "n-x05": {"x": 984, "y": 2355, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "textaudio", "text": "X-05 · Long-press a word in the field to select a range; the style row then applies to that range only. Ranged styles show as underlined spans in the field."},
    "n-u04": {"x": 1476, "y": 3755, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "textaudio", "text": "U-04 · The button reads \"Add beat\" or \"Remove beat\" depending on whether a dot sits under the playhead (±2 frames). Beat dots become snap targets for clips, texts and keyframes."},
    "n-u05": {"x": 1968, "y": 3755, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "textaudio", "text": "U-05 · Tap to record, tap again to stop. The timeline scrolls in real time and a violet bar grows from the start point. Project audio is muted while recording (no headphones needed). Stop creates the voiceover clip and selects it."},
    "n-p03": {"x": 984, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "creative", "text": "P-03 · On preview: drag inside = position, corner handle = size, ↻ handle = rotation, ⇕ arrow handle = feather. Linear/Mirror masks show a line with the same feather arrow."},
    "n-p05": {"x": 1968, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "creative", "text": "P-05 · The diamond button by the playhead adds a keyframe for the selected item (or removes it if the playhead sits on one; it is filled then). Any property change away from a keyframe creates one automatically. Tap a diamond on the bar to jump to it and open easing."},
    "n-s02": {"x": 984, "y": 2355, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "creative", "text": "S-02 · Drawing happens over the frozen frame at the playhead. Done turns the strokes into a PNG sticker that lasts 3 s from the playhead."},
    "n-ex01": {"x": 0, "y": 955, "w": 412, "maxH": 300, "size": "s", "page": "export", "text": "EX-01 · Estimated size recalculates on every change. Unsupported resolutions are queried from the device encoder and shown disabled with a reason on tap. Settings persist as the project's last-used; defaults come from Settings (H-09)."}
  }
}
